# Linked to ~/.config/fd/ignore, the global ignore file fd reads for every search.
#
# The `**/` prefix is required. A pattern that contains a slash is anchored to the directory the
# search started from, so a bare `.git/objects` would only prune a repository sitting exactly at
# that root — never one found further down the tree.
**/.bare/logs
**/.bare/objects
**/.bare/refs
**/.git/logs
**/.git/objects
**/.git/refs
